      "title": "FIS Stock Down Nearly 48% From 52-Week High: Is a Rebound Ahead?",
      "summary": "Fidelity National Information Services (FIS) has declined 48% from its 52-week high amid growth concerns, but improving cash flow and margin expansion offer recovery prospects. Second-quarter free cash flow surged 220% to $525 million, and the Global Payments Issuer Solutions acquisition is expected to add $700 million in free cash flow by 2028. However, lowered 2026 guidance for revenue growth (4.5-5%) and EBITDA growth (5.9-6.9%) highlight ongoing execution challenges. Recovery depends on translating integration benefits into sustainable margin gains and debt reduction rather than rapid revenue acceleration.",
